    {
      "id": "MAT-VEC-M001",
      "subject": "Mathematics",
      "chapter": "Vector Algebra",
      "topic": "Scalar Triple Product Parallelepiped Volume",
      "category": "Vector Algebra :: Advanced Mathematical Structure (Type 1)",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "type": "mcq",
      "question": "Let $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}$ be three non-coplanar vectors in [Vector Algebra]. What is the simplified value of the scalar expression:\n$$[(\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\; (\\vec{b} + \\vec{c}) \\; (\\vec{c} + \\vec{a})]$$",
      "options": [
        "$2 [\\vec{a} \\; \\vec{b} \\; \\vec{c}]$",
        "$[\\vec{a} \\; \\vec{b} \\; \\vec{c}]$",
        "$0$",
        "$4 [\\vec{a} \\; \\vec{b} \\; \\vec{c}]$"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "Expand the scalar triple product: $(\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot [(\\vec{b} + \\vec{c}) \\times (\\vec{c} + \\vec{a})] = (\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot [\\vec{b} \\times \\vec{c} + \\vec{b} \\times \\vec{a} + \\vec{c} \\times \\vec{a}] = [\\vec{a} \\; \\vec{b} \\; \\vec{c}] + [\\vec{b} \\; \\vec{c} \\; \\vec{a}] = 2 [\\vec{a} \\; \\vec{b} \\; \\vec{c}]$.",
      "explanation": "Solve using rigorous mathematical proofs and transformations in Vector Algebra.",
