      "difficulty": "hard",
      "type": "integer",
      "question": "If $\\vec{a} = \\hat{i} + \\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$, $\\vec{b} = \\hat{i} - \\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$, and $\\vec{c} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} - \\hat{k}$ in [Vector Algebra], calculate the integer scalar triple product $[\\vec{a}\\; \\vec{b}\\; \\vec{c}]$.",
      "correctAnswer": 4,
      "solution": "$[\\vec{a}\\; \\vec{b}\\; \\vec{c}] = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\end{vmatrix} = 1(1 - 2) - 1(-1 - 1) + 1(2 - (-1)) = -1 + 2 + 3 = 4$.",
